obs The rebase moved the row twice more, to five moves in all. Peers published %584, %585 and then %586 across three pulls while this commit was being written, so the pkill row took %587 off the fetched spine -- one sed on one site again, and every unlanded citation of mine swept to the stamp rather than to the new number, which is %513's rule applied to my own prose before it lands rather than after.
obs The allocator refused to answer mid-rebase, naming the reason: it counts this tree's in-flight row as taken. That refusal is what kept the fifth renumber honest rather than guessed.
obs A peer had also landed the exact repair my parked lap carried in tools/p/plant_witness.rish -- the adoption floor read from the scan rather than spelled as sourcing=14. Theirs is strictly better and published, so mine was dropped whole. Second time this lap that a peer's version of my own finding arrived first.
